        "geology": "tertiary sandstone banks covered with niveo-aeolean quarternary loam. The tertiary layers surface at the plateau; loam partly covers the slopes; colluvium in the lower valleys within the forest",
        "hydrology": "In the slope, a nutrient-poor aquifer in a tertiary sand-layer results in diffuse springs producing acid nutrient poor water.\r\nIn the colluvial area, nutrient rich water is supplied.\r\nExtensive ecohydrological studies analyse the natural dynamics of the hydrology in this system",
        "soils": null,
        "vegetation": "on the plateau : Fago-Quercetum with Pteridium aquilinum, Convallaria majalis, Maianthemum, etc...\r\non the slope : Stellario- and Primulo-Carpinetum with Anemone nemorosa, Stellaria holostea, Primula elatior, ...\r\nat the nutrient-poor springs in the slope, a nutrient-poor spring forest with facies of Sphagnum species occurs, while in the neutrophylous spring and alluvial zone at the lowest elevations, a species rich alluvial forest (Alno-Padion) occurs, with Allium ursinum, Equisetum telmateia, ..."
